WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.334
-How you doing?
-Doing great.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.501
You look fantastic.
-Thank you. Only for you.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:04.567
-I mean, come on.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.767
-You know I always
make a big effort

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:06.767
when I come on this show.
-You really always do.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.267
I love it.
-I love you, bud.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.267
-You know, helped us out
when we didn't have a show,

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.934
we didn't have an audience,
I was doing it in my home.

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:14.434
-Yeah.
-And you were so cool.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:17.267
You Zoomed in to me in my home,
but I think --

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.767
I want to say
you were the first artist

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.868
to make a performance, a video.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.868
-Yeah, I set up a green screen
in my living room --

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.200
-Yes, you made a whole video.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.367
-For "The Tonight Show,"
and I just couldn't believe it.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.033
I was like, "I can't believe I
have to set up a green screen

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.601
and do this.
-You were the first artist

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:32.901
to do that.
-It was amazing.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.400
-Thank you for doing that.
-It turned out so good.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.734
It's always kind of scary,
you know,

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:38.400
kind of getting in the zone
when it was so new.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.901
-Everyone kind of followed
your thing and started doing

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:42.901
what you were doing, so I can't
thank you enough for that.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:45.901
And congrats on your
Future Nostalgia Tour.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.901
Just played the Garden.
-Yes.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.767
-Oh, my gosh.
The Madison Square Garden.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:50.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.267
Dua!
-Thank you.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.968
-What was it --
Alright, talk to me.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:55.968
-It was surreal.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:59.133
It really exceeded
all my expectations.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:03.534
I think when you go to a place
like New York, you always feel

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:06.234
like maybe people are gonna be
a bit more critical,

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.501
people are gonna, like...
-Sure.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.767
-But everyone just kind of
rode the wave with me.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.934
It was amazing.
They we were all up for it.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.667
The floor was shaking.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.501
-Yeah, when that place --
-It was -- it was brilliant.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.834
It was brilliant. Loved it.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.534
-When Madison Square Garden
rocks, it just rocks.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.701
It's like this studio,
Studio 6B.

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.367
Here we go. This is it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:23.868
It's happening.
-Oh, the floor.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.200
-The floor shakes.
-I can feel it.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.701
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:30.367
-People are talking about
the tour, crazy awesome reviews.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:31.601
Congrats.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:34.367
They love the costumes.
They love the dancing.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:38.367
And on social media, they're
loving one dance in particular.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:40.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:43.334
Yeah, and I love that
you did this 'cause...

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:45.234
Should I explain it,
or do you want to?

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:48.567
-I mean, you can start, and then
I'll, like, riff off it.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.934
-I want to say it was like
in 2017-ish, around that time,

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:56.100
you did a dance that people --
some haters got online

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.133
and said this is a lazy dance
or something, it's uninspired.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.200
-It was kind of like,
"Oh, she looks like she's trying

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.000
to put her shoe on in a rush
or something."

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.133
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.067
-Why do people just
have to be so mean?

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.400
-I think it's okay.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.334
You know, today
when I look back on it --

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.334
and the reason I guess
why we're talking about it

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.000
is 'cause I've brought it back.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.734
I'm doing it on my tour.
-Yeah.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:18.067
-I'm reclaiming it because there
was a moment where, actually,

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.400
it caused me a lot of grief.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.067
Like, I was being bullied
online.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.767
It wasn't very nice.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.267
But -- But now
I'm, like, you know,

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.267
I can look at it
from a different perspective.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.434
I look back on it
with such fondness,

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:32.434
'cause it helped me grow into
the artist I wanted to become.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:36.100
It made me, like, work harder.
I went in, I did more rehearsal.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.934
I just wanted to become
a real performer,

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.767
and I think that was kind of
the thing that I needed.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.934
-And now you open --
is it "Don't Start Now"?

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.667
-Yeah, I start
"Don't Start Now" with it.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:44.901
-With that dance?
-Yep.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.300
-And everyone goes nuts
'cause it's like,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.968
"Yeah, see,
don't make fun of this.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:50.100
Now I'm doing this every show,
so get ready."

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.300
Could you show me the move?

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.133
I'll do it with you.
-Will you do it with me?

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.968
Someone in the audience
was like, "Yeah!"

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:01.100
-Yeah.
-Someone's really excited.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.200
I don't know if I can do it in
these boots, but you know what?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.534
Snow, boots, rain, wind, shine,
whatever.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.200
-You're Dua Lipa.
You can do anything, man.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.701
-Okay.
-Alright.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.033
That's it.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.701
[ Audience cheers ]

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.200
I can't do it.
-Yep. Come on. Come on.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.534
Hip, hip, hip, hip!
-This is embarrassing.

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:19.534
This is me doing it.
That is me doing it.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.000
That is me doing it, by the way.
So bad.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.834
See, that almost hurt me.
That's how old I am.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.501
Oh, my God, how sad?

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.167
But I love that you did that.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.501
I love that you
put it out there.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.767
I just think you're cool.

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.934
I also -- I want to talk
about Elton John

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:39.267
while I can talk to you,

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.667
because that was the greatest
move of all moves.

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:43.667
"Cold Heart."
I'm like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.834
And it went to number one.
-It did.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:49.167
-And, wait, so what's it like
working with Sir Elton?

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.834
-[ Exhales sharply ] It --
I mean, I have so many --

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:54.467
I'm so lucky to have so many
"pinch me" moments in my life.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.534
-Yeah.

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:57.334
-And that's definitely
a massive one.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.667
He's somebody I've looked up to
my whole life.

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:02.968
So to get to do
the song together,

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.300
to re-create his iconic songs --

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.000
-You crushed it, though.
-It's just a massive honor.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.200
I'm so grateful.
And I get to perform it.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.701
-And adding "Rocket Man"
in there, too.

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.367
Like, yo! So good!

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:14.701
-It's just amazing, and I get to
perform it night after night.

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:16.701
And it's just --
it's a dream come true.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.467
I really -- in that moment,

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.467
I really just kind of
soak it all up

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:23.467
and I can't believe everything
that's happening to me.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:27.467
-And then he gave you a very
nice gift, a memorable gift.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:31.634
-He did give me a very lovely,
memorable gift.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:33.801
Sir Elton John put a ring on it.

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.133
-He put --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.467
-[ Laughs ] I'm joking.

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.067
-You're marrying --
-Before this gets into the press

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.400
or whatever --
-You married Elton John?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.567
-No, I didn't.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.067
I didn't, I didn't, I didn't.
-Oh, okay.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.033
-I think David would fight me.

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.534
-Yeah, he would. Of course.
-For sure.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:51.868
-But he gave me a very beautiful
ring that belonged to him,

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:55.367
as just kind of, like, a token

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.701
when we performed together
for the first time.

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.701
And it was just -- I was just --

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:01.267
-How cool is that?
-Yeah.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.934
I keep it...
-I love Elton John.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.067
-I actually kept it at home
locked up in a safe

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:06.901
'cause I just don't think
it was safe back here.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.901
-No, not on our show.
No, no, no, no.

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.067
[ Laughter ]
I'm famous for this.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.901
I want to talk about --
you're always, again,

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:14.734
doing something new
and different.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.901
And you have a new thing
called Service95.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:19.067
It's a concierge newsletter.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:21.067
-Now, that basically means

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:25.067
it tells you cool places to eat
that you've been to,

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.734
it tells you what you're doing
on tour.

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:30.400
It also interviews activists
and people doing stuff

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.734
to change the world.

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:32.901
It's fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:34.400
-I signed up for it.
-Thank you so much.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.767
-Service95.com.

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:37.601
You just type in your email,
boom, off you go.

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:39.934
And it's in 11 different
languages.

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:41.234
-It is, yep.

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:43.067
And our podcast
is also translated

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:44.567
in three different ones.

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:46.868
Hopefully, over time,
we'll get to do more of that.

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:50.367
It's just -- it was really
a platform and a hub

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:53.868
where I could share
so many different sides.

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:55.534
Like, so many different
of my interests,

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:56.868
and things that I felt like

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:59.200
we can all learn
something new from,

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.000
in the process of learning
myself, exploring.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.501
It's all about people
who just want to be

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:05.501
a little bit more curious,

00:06:05.501 --> 00:06:07.834
you know,
kind of putting a mixture,

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.167
from, like you said,
recommendations to...

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.667
-There's art in there.

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:13.000
-There's art, there's music,

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.334
there's fashion,
there's activism.

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:18.801
There's all kinds of articles,
thought provoking...

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:20.634
-It's well done.
-...stories.

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:24.968
And it's just something
where I feel like...

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:27.267
I just want to kind of challenge
people's opinions

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:28.934
and give people
a different perspective

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:31.267
and give people,
different people a voice.

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:35.267
And I just --
I'm enjoying it so much.

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:36.934
It's been so fun to curate it,

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:39.267
and I've got an incredible team
that work with me on it.

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:41.434
-Are you enjoying your podcast,
as well?

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.100
-I'm loving the podcast.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.934
-I mean, "At Your Service."
-It's really fun.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:45.934
Yeah, "At Your Service."

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:47.267
-"At Your Service"
with Dua Lipa.

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:50.601
And you interview everybody.
-Yes, I do.

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:53.434
-You like interviewing people?
-I really do. I really do.

00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:55.434
I really like the research
experience element of it,

00:06:55.434 --> 00:06:57.367
and, like, again, the whole
learning experience

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.000
has been really, really fun.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.901
-Well, you're always up
for something fun.

00:07:00.901 --> 00:07:02.901
Every time you come on the show,
you do something cool.

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:04.734
And tonight we have
a really cool thing

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:06.234
that we're going to try.

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:08.100
You're going to meet
one of your biggest fans.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.434
But we'll talk about this.

00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:10.934
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:11.634
Come on back.

